{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1657 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "228ba5c94f5aec67ce0ebcdd588c0c016f14264d632aaf81ba02012f9b3c75e3" :edb/db-before-t 1656 :edb/db-after-t 1657 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534969 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:52:12.024Z" 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186129169 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446088 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186393194 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/e4/e472070f17c47e78024217ed750690b88de87f3849818368dda1dde5d91d90d4.png)" 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186393194 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/e4/e472070f17c47e78024217ed750690b88de87f3849818368dda1dde5d91d90d4.png)" 13194139534969 17592186045417 false] [17592186403564 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the line $y=x$ and the curve $y={x}^{3},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186403564 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the line $y=x$ and the curve $y={x}^{3},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nI. It is a type I region\nII. It is a type II region\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139534969 17592186045417 false] [17592186403564 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/1d/1d1c1cbe30e6f612f824adc76d712a98194ffccc5edefc11cccdaf07204513ba.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186403564 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/1d/1d1c1cbe30e6f612f824adc76d712a98194ffccc5edefc11cccdaf07204513ba.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534969 17592186045417 false] [17592186446081 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446089 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186446081 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446090 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186446081 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446091 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186446081 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446092 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186446081 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446093 13194139534969 17592186045417 true] [17592186446081 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534969 1